FIRST-TIME SETUP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Create .env file in project root:

   DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"
   SESSION_SECRET="change-this-to-a-long-random-string-in-production"
   KIOSK_IP=          ← tablet/device IP that runs the kiosk (blank = no IP lock)
                       Set to the KIOSK DEVICE's IP, not the server PC's IP.
                       Localhost (127.0.0.1) always bypasses this lock.
   KITCHEN_PIN=1234   ← 4–6 digit staff PIN to access /kitchen page
                       Verified via POST /api/kitchen/auth. Stored in sessionStorage (clears on browser close).
                       Change this before going to production.
   ENABLE_DANGER_ZONE=true  ← set to true in dev only; remove or set false in production
                               Controls visibility of Fresh Start / Load Demo / Nuclear Reset buttons
                               and blocks the /api/system/reset endpoint entirely when false/missing

2. Install dependencies:
   npm install

3. Set up the database:
   npx prisma generate
   npx prisma migrate deploy

   If you get a migration conflict error, resolve it with:
   cmd /c npx prisma migrate resolve --applied 20260412072940_add_order_log

4. Seed the database (loads default menu, admin account, gcash placeholder):
   npx prisma db seed
   Skip this if you want a completely fresh database.

   Default admin login after seed:
   Username: admin
   Password: admin
   ← Change this immediately in production via Admin → Settings → Admin Credentials

5. Run the app (local only):
   npm run dev

