RUNNING ON A LOCAL NETWORK (tablet + PC setup)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Connect the PC and all devices (kiosk tablet, kitchen tablet, queue monitor)
to the same Wi-Fi network.

Run the app so other devices can reach it:
   npm run dev -- -H 0.0.0.0

Find your PC's local IP:
   ipconfig      (Windows) → look for IPv4 Address, e.g. 192.168.1.10

Devices access the system at:
   http://192.168.1.10:3000          ← replace with your actual IP

KIOSK_IP — set to the kiosk tablet's IP (not the server PC's IP):
   When the tablet accesses http://192.168.1.10:3000, the server sees the
   request coming from the tablet's IP. Set KIOSK_IP to the tablet's IP.
   Localhost (127.0.0.1) always bypasses the IP lock so the server PC itself
   can always access the kiosk pages.

   To find tablet IP: Settings → Wi-Fi → tap connected network → IP Address

   Tablet IPs can change on router restart. Set a static IP on the tablet
   or set a DHCP reservation on the router (bind tablet MAC to fixed IP).

